hadiths[30]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1625","Mutamir ibn Sulayman told us, he said: I heard Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Amr ibn Hurayth, from Said ibn Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl, that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The truffle is of the manna, and its water is a cure for the eye."
"1626","Sufyan told us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Amr ibn Hurayth, from Said ibn Zayd, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: The truffle is of the manna, and its water is a cure for the eye."
"1627","Abd al-Samad told us: My father narrated to me: Ata ibn al-Saib told us, from Amr ibn Hurayth, he said: My father narrated to me, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The truffle is of the salwa, and its water is a cure for the eye."
"1628","Sufyan told us, he said: This is what we memorized from al-Zuhri, from Talhah ibn Abdullah ibn Awf, from Said ibn Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever is killed defending his wealth is a martyr, and whoever wrongfully takes a handspan of land will have it hung around him from seven earths."
"1629","Yahya ibn Said told us, from Sadaqah ibn al-Muthanna: My grandfather Riyah ibn al-Harith narrated to me that al-Mughirah ibn Shubah was in the great mosque with the people of Kufah on his right and on his left, then a man called Said ibn Zayd came to him, so al-Mughirah greeted him and seated him at his feet on the couch. Then a man of the people of Kufah came and faced al-Mughirah and reviled and reviled. He said: Whom is this reviling, O Mughirah. He said: He is reviling Ali ibn Abi Talib. He said: O Mughir ibn Shubah, O Mughir ibn Shubah, three times, shall I hear the companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, being reviled in your presence, and you do not object nor change it. For I bear witness upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with what my ears heard and my heart retained from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for I would not narrate a lie from him for which he would question me when I meet him, that he said: Abu Bakr is in Paradise, and Umar is in Paradise, and Ali is in Paradise, and Uthman is in Paradise, and Talhah is in Paradise, and al-Zubayr is in Paradise, and Abd al-Rahman is in Paradise, and Sad ibn Malik is in Paradise, and the ninth of the believers is in Paradise; if I wished I could name him. He said: So the people of the mosque clamored, imploring him: O companion of the Messenger of Allah, who is the ninth. He said: You have implored me by Allah, and by Allah the Almighty, I am the ninth of the believers and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, is the tenth. Then he followed that with an oath. He said: By Allah, a scene witnessed by a man in which his face is dusted along with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, is better than the deed of one of you even if he lived the lifetime of Nuh, peace be upon him."
"1630","Waki told us: Sufyan told us, from Husayn and Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Said ibn Zayd; Waki once said: Mansur, from Said ibn Zayd, and once said: Husayn, from Ibn Zalim, from Said ibn Zayd, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Be still, Hira, for there is upon you none but a prophet or a truthful one or a martyr. He said: And upon it were the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman and Ali and Talhah and al-Zubayr and Sad and Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf and Said ibn Zayd, may Allah be pleased with them."
"1631","Waki told us: Shubah told us, from al-Hurr ibn al-Sayyah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Akhnas, he said: al-Mughirah ibn Shubah addressed us and spoke ill of Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, so Said ibn Zayd stood and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: The Prophet is in Paradise, and Abu Bakr is in Paradise, and Umar is in Paradise, and Uthman is in Paradise, and Ali is in Paradise, and Talhah is in Paradise, and al-Zubayr is in Paradise, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf is in Paradise, and Sad is in Paradise, and if I wished I could name the tenth."
"1632","Umar ibn Ubayd told us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Amr ibn Hurayth, from Said ibn Zayd, he said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: The truffle is of the manna, and its water is a cure for the eye."
"1633","Yahya told us, from Hisham; and Ibn Numayr: Hisham told us: My father narrated to me, from Said ibn Zayd ibn Amr, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him; Ibn Numayr said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever takes a handspan of land wrongfully will have it hung around him on the Day of Resurrection to seven earths. Ibn Numayr said: From seven earths."
"1634","Abd al-Rahman told us: Sufyan told us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Amr ibn Hurayth, from Said ibn Zayd, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out to us with a truffle in his hand and said: Do you know what this is; this is of the manna, and its water is a cure for the eye."
"1635","Muhammad ibn Jafar told us: Shubah told us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, he said: I heard Amr ibn Hurayth, he said: I heard Said ibn Zayd saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: The truffle is of the manna, and its water is a cure for the eye."
"1636","Muhammad ibn Jafar told us: Shubah told us: al-Hakam ibn Utaybah informed me, from al-Hasan al-Urani, from Amr ibn Hurayth, from Said ibn Zayd, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: Shubah said: When al-Hakam narrated it to me I did not reject it as being from the hadith of Abd al-Malik."
"1637","Muhammad ibn Jafar told us: Shubah told us; and Hajjaj: Shubah narrated to me, from al-Hurr ibn Sayyah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Akhnas, that al-Mughirah ibn Shubah addressed and spoke ill of Ali, may Allah be pleased with him. He said: So Said ibn Zayd stood and said: I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: The Messenger of Allah is in Paradise, and Abu Bakr is in Paradise, and Umar is in Paradise, and Ali is in Paradise, and Uthman is in Paradise, and Abd al-Rahman is in Paradise, and Talhah is in Paradise, and al-Zubayr is in Paradise, and Sad is in Paradise. Then he said: If you wish I will inform you of the tenth. Then he mentioned himself."
"1638","Muhammad ibn Jafar told us: Shubah told us, from Husayn, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Abdullah ibn Zalim, he said: al-Mughirah ibn Shubah addressed and spoke ill of Ali, so Said ibn Zayd went out and said: Do you not wonder at this one reviling Ali, may Allah be pleased with him. I bear witness upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that we were upon Hira or Uhud, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Be firm, Hira, or Uhud, for there is upon you only a truthful one or a martyr. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, named the ten; he named Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman and Ali and Talhah and al-Zubayr and Sad and Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, and he named himself, Said."
"1639","Abd al-Razzaq told us: Mamar told us, from al-Zuhri, from Talhah ibn Abdullah ibn Awf, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahl, from Said ibn Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl, that he heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever steals a handspan of land will have it hung around him from seven earths. Mamar said: And it reached me from al-Zuhri, though I did not hear it from him: He added in this hadith: And whoever is killed defending his wealth is a martyr."
"1640","Yazid ibn Harun told us: Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Salamah, that Marwan said: Go and reconcile between these two, Said ibn Zayd and Arwa. So Said said: Do you think I took anything of her right. I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever takes a handspan of land without its right will have it hung around him from seven earths. And whoever takes as patron a freedman of a people without their permission, upon him is the curse of Allah. And whoever seizes the wealth of a Muslim man by oath, may Allah not bless it for him."
"1641","Abu al-Yaman told us: Shuayb told us, from al-Zuhri: Talhah ibn Abdullah ibn Awf narrated to me that Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr ibn Sahl informed him that Said ibn Zayd said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever wrongfully takes a handspan of land will have it hung around him from seven earths."
"1642","Yazid told us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Talhah ibn Abdullah ibn Awf, he said: Arwa bint Uways came to me with a group of Quraysh among whom was Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr ibn Sahl, and she said: Said ibn Zayd has taken from my land into his land what is not his, and I would like you to come to him and speak to him. He said: So we rode to him while he was in his land at al-Aqiq, and when he saw us he said: I have known what brought you, and I will narrate to you what I heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. I heard him saying: Whoever takes of land what is not his will have it hung around him to the seventh earth on the Day of Resurrection. And whoever is killed defending his wealth is a martyr."
"1643","Yazid ibn Abd Rabbihi told us: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid told us: al-Zubaydi narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, from Talhah ibn Abdullah ibn Awf, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr ibn Sahl informed him that Said ibn Zayd said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever wrongfully takes anything of land will have it hung around him from seven earths."
"1644","Ali ibn Asim told us, he said: Husayn informed us, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Abdullah ibn Zalim al-Mazini, he said: When Muawiyah left Kufah he appointed al-Mughirah ibn Shubah. He said: So he set up preachers who fell upon Ali. He said: And I was beside Said ibn Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl. He said: So he became angry and stood and took my hand, and I followed him, and he said: Do you not see this man, unjust to himself, who commands cursing a man of the people of Paradise. So I bear witness upon nine that they are in Paradise, and if I bore witness upon the tenth I would not sin. He said: I said: What is that. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Be firm, Hira, for there is upon you none but a prophet or a truthful one or a martyr. He said: I said: Who are they. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman and Ali and al-Zubayr and Talhah and Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf and Sad ibn Malik. He said: Then he fell silent. He said: I said: And who is the tenth. He said: He said: I am."
"1645","Muawiyah ibn Amr told us: Zaidah told us: Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman told us, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Abdullah ibn Zalim al-Taymi, from Said ibn Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl, he said: I bear witness that Ali is of the people of Paradise. I said: What is that. He said: He is among the nine, and if I wished I could name the tenth. He said: Hira shook, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Be firm, Hira, for there is upon you none but a prophet or a truthful one or a martyr. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Abu Bakr and Umar and Ali and Uthman and Talhah and al-Zubayr and Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf and Sad, and I, meaning Said himself."
"1646","Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas told us: Yunus, or Abu Uways, told us, he said: al-Zuhri said: Talhah ibn Abdullah ibn Awf informed me that Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr ibn Sahl informed him that Said ibn Zayd said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever wrongfully takes anything of land will have it hung around him in seven earths."
"1647","Hammad ibn Usamah told us: Misar informed me, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Abdullah ibn Zalim, from Said ibn Zayd, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, mentioned trials like cuts of dark night; I think he said: People will go therein most swiftly. He said: So it was said: Are all of them destroyed or some of them. He said: Killing will suffice them, or killing suffices them."
"1648","Yazid told us: al-Masudi told us, from Nufayl ibn Hisham ibn Said ibn Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was in Makkah, he and Zayd ibn Harithah, and Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl passed by them, so they invited him to a meal of theirs. He said: O son of my brother, I do not eat of what is slaughtered upon the nusub. He said: And the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was not seen after that eating anything of what was slaughtered upon the nusub. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, my father was as you have seen and as reached you, and if he had met you he would have believed in you and followed you, so seek forgiveness for him. He said: Yes, and I seek forgiveness for him, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection as a nation alone."
"1649","Yazid informed us: Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Salamah, he said: Marwan said to us: Go and reconcile between these two, Said ibn Zayd and Arwa bint Uways. So we came to Said ibn Zayd and he said: Do you think I have taken anything of her right. I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever takes a handspan of land without its right will have it hung around him from seven earths. And whoever takes as patrons a people without their permission, upon him is the curse of Allah. And whoever seizes the wealth of his brother by his oath, may Allah not bless it for him."
"1650","Abu Said told us: Qays ibn al-Rabi told us: Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr told us, from Amr ibn Hurayth, he said: I came to Madinah and I divided property with my brother, and Said ibn Zayd said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No blessing is in the price of land nor a house that is not placed in land nor a house."
"1651","Abu al-Yaman informed us: Shuayb informed us, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Husayn, he said: It reached me that Luqman used to say: O my son, do not learn knowledge to boast thereby against the scholars, or to dispute thereby with the fools, and to show off thereby in gatherings. Then he mentioned it and said: Nawfal ibn Musahiq narrated to us, from Said ibn Zayd, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Of the greatest usury is attacking the honor of a Muslim without right. And this kinship is a branch from al-Rahman, so whoever cuts it, Allah forbids Paradise to him."
"1652","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi told us: Ibrahim ibn Sad told us, from his father, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Muhammad ibn Ammar ibn Yasir, from Talhah ibn Abdullah ibn Awf, from Said ibn Zayd, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever is killed defending his wealth is a martyr, and whoever is killed defending his family is a martyr, and whoever is killed defending his religion is a martyr, and whoever is killed defending his blood is a martyr."
"1653","Yaqub told us: My father told us, from his father, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Muhammad ibn Ammar, from Talhah ibn Abdullah ibn Awf, from Said ibn Zayd, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he mentioned the like of it."
"1654","al-Fadl ibn Dukayn told us: Israil told us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir: One who heard Amr ibn Hurayth narrating from Said ibn Zayd narrated to me, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: O assembly of Arabs, praise Allah Who has lifted the tithes from you."
